ert ratings.", "Incumbent Aaron Bean (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Aaron Bean, the Republican incumbent, seeks reelection in a northeastern Florida district that leans Republican by about five points. He holds a decisive financial advantage, having raised over $2.1 million and retaining $1.6 million on hand, while Democratic nominee LaShonda Holloway raised roughly $27,000 after a contested primary. No independent general-election polling is available for the race.\n\nExpert raters broadly place the seat in Republican territory, with several calling it solid or safe Republican and others likely Republican, and prediction markets price Bean's chances near 86 percent. The forecast expects Bean to win by roughly ten points, with Holloway needing an unusually favorable environment and resources she currently lacks to make this competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0948, "margin": -8.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0811, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0937, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0773, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0859, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0659, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0699, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0664, "margin": -10.0}]}